WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.235
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody!

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:05.704
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-What a crowd.

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:07.106
-That's fantastic.
-It feels great.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.541
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.909
Well, guys,
this is very exciting.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.513
Today, New York lowered
the COVID vaccine eligibility

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.281
to 50 years old.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.117
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.753
So good news --
now every New York City hot dog

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.155
can get the vaccine.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.556
-Aww.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.725
-Yep, New Yorkers will do
anything to get vaccinated.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.862
This morning, I saw Times Square
Elmo getting gray streaks.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.730
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.502
He was wearing a mask.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.037
-Yeah, that's true.
-Yeah. Technically.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.173
Dropping the age requirement
to 50 is super-exciting

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:43.610
until you go for your shot
and no one checks your ID.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.778
It's like --
"Don't you want to see proof?"

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.647
It's like, "No.
You're -- You're fine."

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:50.316
My mom would do that
all the time.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.685
Like, "I got my ID checked
today at the store."

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:57.991
I go, "They didn't think
you were 21 years old?"

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.825
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:02.528
She really did do that.
Oh, gosh.

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.663
Honestly, this really means
that everyone's eligible

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:07.066
'cause, after the last year,
even kids look 50.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.367
[Inhales sharply]

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.036
[Gravelly voice]
"What do I have to do

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:13.406
to get a Go-Gurt around here?"

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.140
Meanwhile, today in Russia,
Vladimir Putin

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.809 line:0%
got his COVID vaccine,

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.546 line:0%
but the Kremlin wouldn't say
which vaccine Putin got.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.779
-Ooh.

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:24.283
-Yep, it will either be
Sputnik V, COVID-Vac,

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:27.387
or Smirnoff &amp; Smirnoff.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:30.556
The nurse asked which arm,
and Putin said, "Left pec,"

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.759
and then galloped away
shirtless on a horse.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.295
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.829
Yep, by getting the vaccine,

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:39.198
Putin made history
as the first Russian

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.634
to get injected with something
and live to talk about it.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:45.237
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:46.672
I mean, normally,
when a Russian

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.508
gets injected,
they're either being poisoned

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:51.010
or preparing for the Olympics.
Let's be honest.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.613
-[ Audience groans ]
-Woman: Nice!

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.648
-[ Laughs ]
I got a "nice" on that.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.982
-Wow. "Nice!"
-Somebody said, "Nice!"

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:59.752
That's the thing about
these tinier, smaller crowds.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.187
-They're intimate.
-Yeah, they're actual --

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.389
Verbal feedback.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:07.159
-"Nice!" All right.
I'll take "nice."

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.196
Speaking of the pandemic,
I saw that DoorDash will now

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.699
deliver COVID test kits
to your house.

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:16.435
Yeah, the DoorDash guy
will hook you up with fast food,

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.539
COVID tests, and, after
a long enough pause, weed.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:23.176
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.011
"Here's your delivery.
Here's your test.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.212
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:30.850
All right. All right.
Let me see what I got."

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.618
I got to be honest.
It's a little strange

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:34.420
getting medical supplies
from the same guy

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.956
who bought you lunch
from Fuddruckers.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.292
Get this.
I saw that the theme park

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.728
Disney California Adventure
just reopened.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:44.697
That's right. You can pay $75

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.532
to walk around the park
and buy stuff,

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:50.169
but none of the rides
are running.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.338
The CEO of Disneyland was
on the news to talk about it.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.639 line:0%
Check it out.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.107 line:0%
-We're certainly
going to be operating

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:57.310 line:0%
under some significant
capacity constraints,

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.779 line:0%
but there's still plenty
of things you can do at the park

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.481 line:0%
like...

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.063
Ohh. That sounds --
That sounds fun.

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.799
"Hey. Hey.
We're on the tea cups.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.101
We're on the tea cups!"

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.136
Some news --

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:25.838
Some news out of Washington
this week.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.175
President Biden's team
is working on a $3-trillion

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.978 line:0%
proposal for jobs, education,
and infrastructure.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.080 line:0%
Yeah. $3 trillion.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.383
Does Joe Biden have a bunch
of bitcoin we don't know about?

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.352
Yep, the plan
will cost $3 trillion,

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.287
and it will be paid for
in quarters

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.122
Biden finds behind your ear.

00:03:44.122 --> 00:03:46.025
"Hey, whippersnapper."

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.927
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.628
Actually, to pay for his plan,

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:53.232
Biden may raise taxes
on corporations.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.401
And you can tell
big corporations aren't happy.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.603
This morning, when Biden asked
his iPhone for the weather,

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.305
Siri was like...

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.040
-Siri:
Try opening a window, bitch.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.976
-Ohh! Indeed!

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.078
[ Applause ]

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:07.913
That is rude!

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:10.383
-This was interesting.
According to the White House,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:14.753 line:0%
Biden and former President Obama
talk on the phone all the time.

00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:16.556 line:0%
Yeah, it's strange
when those guys talk.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.257 line:0%
Half the time,
the other is thinking,

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:21.326 line:0%
"Will this guy
wrap it up already?"

00:04:21.326 --> 00:04:23.429
Biden and Obama actually
have a great relationship,

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.131
I mean, compared
to the last president,

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.467
who tried to have
his VP murdered!

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.602
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.640
Some business news. I saw that
Popeyes just announced plans

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.910
to open its first restaurant
in the UK.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.346
Oh, man, the monarchy is already
on the brink of collapse.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:45.118
I don't think they can handle
a chicken-sandwich war.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.553
Yeah, at long last, people
of the UK will be able to taste

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.723
that exotic delicacy --
chicken on bread.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.592
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:55.527
[British accent]
"My word, what do you call this?

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:56.996
-[British accent]
"Insane!

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.064
-This isn't a scone at all!

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:01.167
-Someone call
the Earl of Surrey!"

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.635
-It's a buttermilk biscuit!"

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:05.771
-"Wait. This chicken is fried!"

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:08.474
-Listen to this.
There's a new study

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.175
that found that, on average,

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:13.412
people gained 2 pounds per month
during quarantine.

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:14.914
Keep in mind,
some of that weight

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.415
is just layers of sweatpants

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:19.185
that are now melded
to your body.

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:20.653
People are like, "Whoa. Hang on.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:25.091
I got injected with the vaccine.
That's got to weigh something."

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.059
We all knew something was up
because over the last year

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:29.562
either our masks got smaller
or our faces got bigger.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.330
Do you know
what I'm talking about?

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.598
And, finally, this is crazy.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.666
A Utah man's
Ring doorbell camera

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:37.903
captured four cougars
outside his front door.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:41.073
Take a look at this.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:42.742
Look at that.

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:48.680
Yeah. When he looked back later,
he saw an empty pizza box

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.150
and a torn red shirt
that said "Papa John's."

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.353
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.124
You know when I heard
about four cougars on a camera,

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.625
I thought it was
going to be the trailer

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.361
for the new "Sex and the City."

